s of the galaxy holiday special  armor wars coming to disney plus iron  heart coming to disney plus  secret invasion moon knight she-hulk and  the hawkeye series coming to disney plus  and captain marvel 2.  a new recap series called marvel legends  which already has the first two episodes  out about wanda and vision and  the fantastic four and on top of that we  do have some projects that were revealed  to be in development at marvel studios  projects that have not been announced  yet to the general public by marvel and  these films or  disney plus shows it's not clarified are  nova  secret warriors ghost writer the  illuminati  nomad and the young avengers so how  exactly is all of this going to come  together in marvel's plans  well there are six very important  milestones that marvel is going to go  through until we eventually get to that  avengers in-game event again  and if you're wondering if marvel really  does have the next five to ten years  planned out  yes they do and kevin feige has recently  confirmed that kevin feige recently said  in an interview to varying degrees of  specificity  it's always about five to six years out  versus what we've announced  so whatever that takes us to now marvel  studios has announced films  up to what we estimate to be 2023 so  add five to six years to that marvel  studios has planned out the mcu to about  2028  or 2029 and they're going to be many  different movies and  shows coming out from marvel studios but  again it's going to hang on six  major points and the first one of those  six major events  is the introduction of the x-men this is  going to be a huge milestone for  marvel studios fox no longer owns the  x-men properties  disney and marvel studios does and  they're now going to incorporate them  into their super successful  interconnected universe known as  the mcu the marvel cinematic universe  now as far as how the x-men  are going to be introduced and built up  all evidence points to  mutants being introduced before the  actual x-men  team some individual mutants will kind  of get their own stories  until we are eventually introduced to  the actual x-men team  and it looks like the x-men are going to  be introduced a lot sooner than we  thought  and this was revealed by the one and  only marvel studios president kevin  feige in a recent interview  in the interview he was asked this  question we know with monica rambo in  one division  her character connects into captain  marvel 2 and that series connects to  doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness  is one division a ramp to the revival of  x-men your planning in which he replied  in hindsight in five years if when we're  talking about everything that's happened  everything can be a ramp to everything  specifically though  yes monica and captain marvel 2 and  specifically to wanda  teaming up with doctor strange in the  multiverse of madness  so kevin feige himself kind of did just  confirm that the x-men are going to  start to be set up as early on as in the  one division series  now there's a lot of speculation and  theories that we could go through on how  this actually happens and i will but in  other videos  the bottom line here is that the x-men  are going to be a huge staple of the  marvel cinematic universe and ultimately  be a part of marvel's main  plan the next huge milestone for the  marvel cinematic universe is  going to be the introduction of the  fantastic four now the fantastic four  are going to be introduced  differently than the x-men the x-men are  going to be introduced one-on-one and  then come together as a group but the  fantastic four are going to be  introduced  as a group together then periodically in  the mcu they're going to work with other  heroes and other groups randomly  now of course in the mcu it's not going  to be random it's going to be  grouped together by a series of events  but they're going to work here and there  with  different people and different groups  spider-man possibly doctor strange  bruce banner she hulk and of course some  of the x-men as well  and actually the fantastic four and one  division share  one thing in common and that is agatha  harkness in the comics not only does  agatha harkness at one point teach wanda  how to grow  and harness her powers she is also the  babysitter and watcher of franklin  richards the son  of sue storm and reed richards the  invisible woman and mr fantastic so  everything is connected the next major  milestone is going to be the next  avengers team who we refer to right now  as the new avengers  now of course there are going to be new  characters introduced that we don't know  about yet that will join the new  avengers and of course there are going  to be characters that we already know  who are going to be a part of the team  as well such as sam and bucky  hopefully the scarlet witch if  everything works out for her doctor  strange  spider-man captain marvel and hopefully  more then another major milestone is  going to be the young avengers  now at this point we pretty much know  who the young avengers team is going to  be  and it's going to get started with one  division with wanda and visions twin  boys  wiccan and speed we've seen them in the  previews already so they're coming in a  couple of days  then you have people like cassie lang  scott lang's daughter who could go on to  be stature  kate bishop miss marvel harley keener  from iron man 3 and at the end of  avengers end game there  and hopefully a few more this is going  to be huge because it's another avengers  team and they're going to take on very  different villains than the new avengers  the x-men and the fantastic four  and speaking of villains the villains  are going to be the fifth major  milestone of marvel studios we have one  major villain coming that marvel studios  has already confirmed and another  insanely huge villain that marvel has  already teased  but they haven't come out and said who  it is yet and these two 